  "id": "catalepsy",
  "term": "catalepsy",
  "definition": "Catalepsy is a state of marked inactivity and reduced response to stimulation, with a tendency to hold a fixed posture. A person’s limbs may stay in whatever position they are placed, sometimes called waxy flexibility, and this state can occur with psychotic disorders, drug toxicity affecting the nervous system, or other conditions.",
